        <p>Narvous disorders are generally traceable to defective digestion. Most nervous people are dyspeptic also. The stomach does not digest the food ; the necessary 3upply of vital particles which the blood should receiv, from properly digested food fails, and the result is felt almost immediately upon the most sensitive portions of the human organism—the nerves. Impure blood irritates the nerves and causes nervous weakness. This renders the nervous system very liable to be affected by unhealthy influences. In nine cases out:of ten, if the imperfect digestion be remedied, the nervousness and weakness wilt disappear. The only certain remedy is wilym Evans' Qainine Bitters, sold everywhere in bottles as. 91 and 4s. 61 each, or will be sent, carriage free, on receipt of stamps, direct, by the Sole Propriet- ors :—Tbd Quinine ilitters Manufacturing Company, Limited. Llanelly, South Wales. Beware of Imita- tions. The name " Gwilym vans";d must be found on 'the label, on the stamp, and on the bottle, to ensure its being genuine. Be sure you get the right article when - you ask for it. Do not be put off with substitutes. No ther preparation is " Just as good "or " Tile same</p>
