        <p>„tr• I.W. Reader, a Liverpool lay preacher, has treided gift for epigram. He read apaper at 'Pool the Other day on "Preaching.” "Some j:a.,(liors," ha said, "aim at nothing, and sue- hitting it. Their excellency is that hav,o no .faults, and their fault that they no excAllencies." Mr. Reader added that i,.,_ertuons should not be long, for if they are .(1 they need not be long, .ancl if they are 41(1 they Ought not to be."</p>
